  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="NL">National appeal &apos;Help slachtoffers aardbeving&apos; (support victims earthquake T&#xfc;rkiye and Syria)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On Monday, February 6, a terrible disaster completely changed the lives of millions of people in Turkey and Syria. Multiple powerful earthquakes and aftershocks caused massive damage. More than 50,000 people died and many others were injured. At least 2.7 million people were left homeless. 
Many people not only lost friends or relatives, but also lost their homes and belongings. Many people also lost their source of income; they can no longer work because their clients have left for a safer area or because the building where they were working collapsed.

Currently, the focus of aid is on providing temporary shelter, medical care and food and drink. The organisations also distribute relief items such as hygiene kits, winter clothing and blankets. There is also a focus on psychosocial support and safe places are created for children to learn and play.

In the coming period, the relief effort will look different. Many people who are now temporarily housed in a tent will soon move to a container house. People who can cook for themselves will then receive food parcels instead of meals. In addition, financial support will be extended. People will receive help through cash and can use it to buy the things they need most at the time.</narrative>
  </description>
